(a) Intergovernmental agreements. If another county, municipality, or user located within another municipality or county contributes wastewater to the authority's wastewater system, the authority shall enter into an intergovernmental agreement with the respective municipality or county that is contributing or within which a user is contributing and shall revise the service delivery strategy if necessary.
(b) Required information. Prior to entering into an agreement required by subsection (a) of this section, the director shall request the following information from the contributing municipality:
(1) A description of the quality and volume of wastewater discharged to the authority's wastewater system by the contributing jurisdiction;
(2) An inventory of all users located within the contributing municipality that are discharging to the authority's wastewater system;
(3) Such other information as the director may deem necessary.
(c) Contents of an intergovernmental sewer agreement. An intergovernmental agreement, as required by subsection (a) of this section, shall contain the following conditions:
(1) A requirement for the contributing jurisdiction to adopt a sewer use article which is at least as stringent as this article with prohibited discharges and local maximum allowable limits that are at least as stringent as those set out in division 2 of this article. The requirement shall specify that such ordinance and limits must be revised as necessary to reflect changes made to this division or local limits;
(2) A requirement for the contributing jurisdiction to submit a revised user inventory on at least an annual basis;
(3) A provision specifying which pretreatment implementation activities, including wastewater discharge permit issuance, inspection and sampling, and enforcement, will be conducted by the contributing jurisdiction; which of these activities will be conducted by the director; and which of these activities will be conducted jointly by the contributing jurisdiction and the director;
(4) A requirement for the contributing jurisdiction to provide the director with access to all information that the contributing jurisdiction obtains as part of its pretreatment activities;
(5) Limits on the nature, quality, and volume of the contributing jurisdiction's wastewater at the point where it discharges to the authority's wastewater system;
(6) Requirements for monitoring the contributing jurisdiction's discharge;
(7) For those users that are not the jurisdiction itself, a provision ensuring the director access to the facilities of contributing nonresidential users located within the contributing jurisdiction's boundaries for the purpose of inspection, sampling, and any other duties deemed necessary by the director; and
(8) A provision specifying remedies available for breach of the terms of the intergovernmental agreement.
(Res. No. 2005-55, art. I(7), 9-15-2005)

